# Charon screen reader settings (Linux companion program of the Charon speaking
# UEFI boot manager and pre-boot screen reader). GPL-2.0-or-later.
#
# Changes, from the running system, what Charon otherwise changes in its own
# pre-boot menu: the settings record \EFI\HAK\charon-settings-a.bin / -b.bin on
# the EFI system partition, the reader add-on (driver option "Charon voice")
# and the reader-only marker.
#
# Python 3.6 or newer, standard library only. Plain line-oriented text
# interface (numbered menus, one prompt per line, no curses, no cursor
# addressing) for Speakup, Fenrir, Orca and braille displays in a terminal.
#
# Options: --esp DIR (a folder standing in for the EFI partition), --no-firmware
# (never touch firmware variables), --firmware-dir DIR (test stand-in for the
# firmware variables, efivarfs file format), --lang en|pl, --show, --synths, --set
# member=value, --defaults, --repair, --format X, --reader-only on|off,
# --addon on|off|status, --yes, --version. Without them: the interactive menu.
#
# The tables below are the shared specification of the record (the Windows
# program Charon-Settings.ps1 carries the same ones).
